# ACRe CRM — local environment variables
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values, then:
#   source .env && python run.py

# Required: password to log in to the CRM
CRM_PASSWORD=your-shared-password-here

# Optional: secret key for Flask sessions (auto-generated if not set)
# SECRET_KEY=some-random-string

# ── Shared database (so all teammates see the same data) ───────────────────────
#
# By default the app uses a local SQLite file (crm.db).
# To share data with coworkers, point everyone at the same PostgreSQL database.
#
# Free options:
#   - Neon       https://neon.tech      (generous free tier, instant setup)
#   - Supabase   https://supabase.com   (free tier, also has a dashboard)
#   - Render     https://render.com     (free PostgreSQL, 90-day expiry on free plan)
#
# After creating a database, paste the connection string here:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/dbname
#
# Leave this line commented out to use local SQLite instead.
